I go into the places where...

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.600
First of all, it's a
little bit mind blowing

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:53.630
if you've never been there,

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:55.760
for Locke it was really mind blowing

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:57.380
to just walk up and down this street

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:00.570
and literally every single
restaurant has got a person,

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.190
a band playing music, right?

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:04.092
Yeah, including Taco Bell, seriously.

00:22:04.092 --> 00:22:08.000
Now, a lot of it is very bad.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:12.210
I would say the majority of the music

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:14.520
that I heard coming out of
those places is pretty bad.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.600
I'm not a huge fan of
modern country in general.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:18.500
It gets better the later you stay.

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:22.125
But you go to a place where there's guys,

00:22:22.125 --> 00:22:24.977
somebody's got gray hair and you're like,

00:22:24.977 --> 00:22:26.220
"That's a good sign."

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.100
There's a dude who's playing a pedal steel

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:31.420
who looks like this may
be his last time ever

00:22:31.420 --> 00:22:34.440
playing the pedal steel or
he may die while on stage.

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:35.604
Yeah.

00:22:35.604 --> 00:22:37.740
And also there's hardly
anybody in there watching

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:39.560
except some other old people.

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:40.877
I saw that place and I was like,

00:22:40.877 --> 00:22:42.240
"This is where we need to go."

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.490
We go inside, over the
course of like five songs

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:47.210
they played three Merle Haggard songs.

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:49.060
Do you remember which one it was?

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:51.410
I can't remember the place
that was our favorite

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:53.220
from when we played at the Ryman.

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.450
I don't remember the name
of the place, honestly.

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:56.623
It is a woman's name.

00:22:57.556 --> 00:23:00.140
But it was towards the river

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:02.247
and pretty close to like
the Glen Campbell Museum

00:23:02.247 --> 00:23:03.550
and a little road you go off

00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:04.960
to get to the Johnny Cash Museum,

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:06.140
which I didn't go into.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:08.520
We just kind of took a
picture for Shepherd...

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:12.090
And they would let Locke
in there, under age?

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:13.630
Dude, there's no rules, man.

00:23:13.630 --> 00:23:14.463
Okay.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.180
In fact the waitress offered him a beer.

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:20.550
I mean, he doesn't look 17, he looks...

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:21.383
No.

00:23:21.383 --> 00:23:23.360
And I was like, "Ah, let's not do that."

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:27.760
So we did that but then it
was all about the hot chicken.

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:29.940
Yeah, I'm curious, where did you go?

00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:32.760
So my experience, the
first time I ever had

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.160
authentic Nashville hot chicken,

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:36.238
which a lot of people are like,

00:23:36.238 --> 00:23:38.200
"You talking about spicy chicken?"

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:39.660
Hopefully, if you've watched
Good Mythical Morning,

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:41.760
you know the hot chicken
is not spicy chicken.

00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:42.970
It is his own category,

00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:44.580
it's not like the spicy chicken sandwich

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:46.370
you get at McDonald's, okay?

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:49.300
This is a very specific
recipe and it's very good

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:50.630
and it's one of my favorite things.

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.620
The breading is very red.

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:56.160
Yeah, it has a lot of spice
mixed into the breading

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:58.960
and then it's got like
a coating of like dry,

00:23:58.960 --> 00:24:01.330
but also a little bit wet,
you've got to just have it.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:05.280
So the best I've ever had
is Hattie B's in Nashville

00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:09.000
but I had even heard that that Hattie B's

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.920
was not the originator of hot chicken.

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:13.680
We were told, when we went there,

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:17.473
that Bolton's Hot Chicken
and Fish was the originator

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:22.110
and we went there and
it was very, very good.

00:24:22.110 --> 00:24:23.100
Very down-home.

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.760
But it turns out that
that's also not true.

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:27.800
Bolton's is not the first person to do it.

00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:30.710
The first place to do it
is Prince's Hot Chicken.

00:24:30.710 --> 00:24:33.420
I never even heard of
Prince's Hot Chicken,

00:24:33.420 --> 00:24:34.300
but I'm telling...

00:24:34.300 --> 00:24:36.600
I told you about Prince's Hot Chicken.

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:38.290
I thought you told me about Bolton's.

00:24:38.290 --> 00:24:41.270
No, no, no, when I took the kids

00:24:41.270 --> 00:24:45.260
to the wedding in Nashville
last year, we went to Prince's.

00:24:45.260 --> 00:24:47.280
Did you go to the one in Assembly Hall

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.380
or did you go to the original location?

00:24:48.380 --> 00:24:52.108
It was on, I think the original
location after the fire,

00:24:52.108 --> 00:24:54.690
not the original, original,
it was in a strip mall.

00:24:54.690 --> 00:24:56.790
We waited way too long for it.

00:24:56.790 --> 00:24:58.940
Well, I blocked that out of my mind

00:24:58.940 --> 00:25:00.450
and I probably about to tell you something

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:02.450
that you already know,
but just let me tell you.

00:25:02.450 --> 00:25:07.170
So Assembly Hall is like
sort of like a food court

00:25:07.170 --> 00:25:08.960
on steroids, a mall.

00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:10.080
Oh, near downtown?

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:12.950
Right across the street from the Ryman.

00:25:12.950 --> 00:25:14.220
Yeah.

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:15.053
That's where you went?

00:25:15.053 --> 00:25:15.970
There's a Prince's there?

00:25:15.970 --> 00:25:16.803
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:25:16.803 --> 00:25:17.990
There's a Hattie B's there.

00:25:17.990 --> 00:25:19.097
It's new, there wasn't when you went

00:25:19.097 --> 00:25:20.055
There wasn't when I went.

00:25:20.055 --> 00:25:21.375
Okay, all right, so...

00:25:21.375 --> 00:25:23.190
But I went to the Hattie B's there,

00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:25.560
which it must be right in the same place.

00:25:25.560 --> 00:25:28.520
The Prince's is upstairs
in the food court area,

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:30.040
Hattie B's is down in the outdoor mall.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:32.150
So, you went for Prince's.

00:25:32.150 --> 00:25:35.227
Okay, Locke and I got into
this discussion and I was like,

00:25:35.227 --> 00:25:36.480
"Listen, I'm going to tell you right now,

00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:39.800
I've never had better hot
chicken than Hattie B's,

00:25:39.800 --> 00:25:41.549
but I've also never had Prince's

00:25:41.549 --> 00:25:44.400
and everyone is saying that
princess is the original place."

00:25:44.400 --> 00:25:46.840
And then we go online and we're looking at

00:25:46.840 --> 00:25:48.270
all these lists of the places

00:25:48.270 --> 00:25:49.130
that you should have hot chicken

00:25:49.130 --> 00:25:50.507
and list after list is like,

00:25:50.507 --> 00:25:52.880
"Go to Prince's Hot for the original.

00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:55.640
Everyone is just trying to
imitate that, it's true."

00:25:55.640 --> 00:25:57.700
So I was like, "Well, okay,

00:25:57.700 --> 00:25:59.750
I mean, it's not going to be
a disappointing experience.

00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:01.696
I mean, it may not be
as good as Hattie B's,

00:26:01.696 --> 00:26:04.770
side-by-side comparison or whatever."

00:26:04.770 --> 00:26:05.847
But the thing that
Locke said, he was like,

00:26:05.847 --> 00:26:09.307
"Dad, but there's a lot of
people in line at Hattie B's

00:26:09.307 --> 00:26:12.000
and there's not a lot of
people in line at Prince's.

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.729
And I was like, "well,
that's just because it's like

00:26:13.729 --> 00:26:15.900
it's upstairs in this place

00:26:15.900 --> 00:26:18.647
and Hattie B's is a better location."

00:26:19.540 --> 00:26:21.157
But I was also like,

00:26:21.157 --> 00:26:22.650
"Okay, you just tell me
which one you want to do."

00:26:22.650 --> 00:26:24.870
And he was like, "I think
we should go to the place

00:26:24.870 --> 00:26:26.100
that has more people at it."

00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:28.209
And I was like, "But
what about the original?"

00:26:28.209 --> 00:26:30.440
I take full responsibility for this

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:32.600
because I talked him
into going to Prince's.

00:26:32.600 --> 00:26:33.874
Dad said, "Do you want to get the best

00:26:33.874 --> 00:26:34.740
or do you want to get the original?"

00:26:34.740 --> 00:26:35.700
I said, "Let's get the best."

00:26:35.700 --> 00:26:37.140
He's like, "We've got
to get the original."

00:26:37.140 --> 00:26:38.546
We got it, it pretty shit.

00:26:38.546 --> 00:26:39.536
It wasn't bad.

00:26:39.536 --> 00:26:40.369
It was bad.

00:26:40.369 --> 00:26:42.103
It was bad.

00:26:42.103 --> 00:26:44.450
I can't believe it, I did the same thing.

00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:46.890
But you got to rectify it.

00:26:46.890 --> 00:26:48.820
Yeah, I went to Hattie B's the next day.

00:26:48.820 --> 00:26:52.090
Well, I wasn't able to do
that because I had to leave.

00:26:52.090 --> 00:26:53.713
Let me just tell you right now.

00:26:55.070 --> 00:26:57.230
Once I got up there and
we put our order in,

00:26:57.230 --> 00:26:59.829
and by the way, we also got T-shirts

00:26:59.829 --> 00:27:01.710
that said Prince's Hot Chicken

00:27:01.710 --> 00:27:02.543
because I'm working a T-shirt

00:27:02.543 --> 00:27:04.580
and I've got a hat at Biscuit Head,

00:27:04.580 --> 00:27:06.437
we're getting memorabilia
all over the place,

00:27:06.437 --> 00:27:07.580
this is just what the
road trip's all about.

00:27:07.580 --> 00:27:09.020
It's a good idea.

00:27:09.020 --> 00:27:12.950
So, we order a couple of

00:27:12.950 --> 00:27:15.710
medium hot chicken sandwiches,

00:27:15.710 --> 00:27:18.140
so typically medium is like super hot,

00:27:18.140 --> 00:27:19.518
if you have any experience
with hot chicken.

00:27:19.518 --> 00:27:22.390
The hot it's like harder
than anyone can handle

00:27:22.390 --> 00:27:23.576
and there's two levels above that

00:27:23.576 --> 00:27:24.800
and it's just kind of like comical

00:27:24.800 --> 00:27:26.140
to even think about typically.

00:27:26.140 --> 00:27:26.973
Yeah.

00:27:26.973 --> 00:27:29.735
So, I noticed that there's
a lot of people in line.

00:27:29.735 --> 00:27:32.310
There's a lot of people waiting,
not only people in line,

00:27:32.310 --> 00:27:33.270
but a lot of people waiting.

00:27:33.270 --> 00:27:34.210
And then at that point

00:27:34.210 --> 00:27:36.140
is when I go to the specific Yelp reviews,

00:27:36.140 --> 00:27:38.430
not for Prince's, but for
this Prince's location,

00:27:38.430 --> 00:27:40.671
which is like not in
the original location,

00:27:40.671 --> 00:27:43.456
it's like the mall location,
for lack of a better word.

00:27:43.456 --> 00:27:45.620
Yeah, it's a tourist trap downtown.

00:27:45.620 --> 00:27:47.610
And I begin to get a sinking feeling

00:27:47.610 --> 00:27:48.443
because people are like,

00:27:48.443 --> 00:27:50.810
"This place is so poorly managed.

00:27:50.810 --> 00:27:53.400
It's not going to be
representative of hot chicken.

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:55.610
It's just a piece of
chicken with some sauce,

00:27:55.610 --> 00:27:57.390
kind of dollops on it."

00:27:57.390 --> 00:27:58.997
And then I'm there
saying, these people are,

00:27:58.997 --> 00:28:00.020
"There's no way it's that bad."

00:28:00.020 --> 00:28:02.616
There's no way a place
that has this reputation

00:28:02.616 --> 00:28:04.210
is letting this happen.

00:28:04.210 --> 00:28:05.120
I mean, it's not going to be bad,

00:28:05.120 --> 00:28:05.953
I mean, the worst,

00:28:05.953 --> 00:28:08.360
it's just going to be a
good fried chicken sandwich.

00:28:08.360 --> 00:28:10.930
It was the most disappointing
culinary experience

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:12.560
I've ever had in my entire life.

00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:14.680
Man, I wish you would
have gone just downstairs

00:28:14.680 --> 00:28:15.855
to the Hattie B's right afterwards.

00:28:15.855 --> 00:28:16.960
Well, the line at Hattie B's...

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:18.430
Well, remember what I told you

00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:20.410
because it was so good.

00:28:20.410 --> 00:28:22.540
I wasn't sure that you Prince's.

00:28:22.540 --> 00:28:24.170
It's touristy.

00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:27.580
I mean, everything in
that area is for tourists,

00:28:27.580 --> 00:28:32.580
but Hattie B's, they've
optimized the tourist experience

00:28:33.470 --> 00:28:35.070
with some of the things that they offer.

00:28:35.070 --> 00:28:37.259
Well, but it's also, it's just good.

00:28:37.259 --> 00:28:38.092
It's so good.

00:28:38.092 --> 00:28:40.144
It's good and it's consistent.

00:28:40.144 --> 00:28:43.030
And so lesson learned
for me, first of all,

00:28:43.030 --> 00:28:44.610
I had to apologize profusely to Locke,

00:28:44.610 --> 00:28:47.520
we ended up getting like some
Jennie's ice cream after.

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:50.350
I almost was like, "Let's just
go and get right back in line

00:28:50.350 --> 00:28:51.410
and just get Hattie B's."

00:28:51.410 --> 00:28:53.020
But that line was probably an hour long

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:55.760
and we kind of were tired
and wanted to go to bed.

00:28:55.760 --> 00:28:58.540
But, I can't speak for the
original Prince's location

00:28:58.540 --> 00:29:01.520
but if the Prince's enterprise is allowing

00:29:01.520 --> 00:29:03.819
any location to be as horrible

00:29:03.819 --> 00:29:07.720
as the one in Assembly
Hall, then I'm never going.

00:29:07.720 --> 00:29:10.840
I will never go, you lost your opportunity

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:12.400
to gain me as a fan.

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:16.160
Hattie B's is amazing, and
Bolton's is really good,

00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:18.000
but Hattie B's is the standard.

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.590
You shouldn't go to the
place that created it,

00:29:20.590 --> 00:29:22.320
you should go to the
place that perfected it,

00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:23.772
and they have perfected it.

00:29:23.772 --> 00:29:26.420
At least for tourists, I totally agree.

00:29:26.420 --> 00:29:29.470
By the way, there's a hip-hop
theme pizza restaurant

00:29:29.470 --> 00:29:33.930
right across the way from
it in that same thoroughfare

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:35.520
and I recommend that place too.

00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:37.510
Well, if I had to spent multiple days.

00:29:37.510 --> 00:29:38.730
I mean, next time I come through

00:29:38.730 --> 00:29:39.563
I know what I'm doing.

00:29:39.563 --> 00:29:41.130
They've got cinnamon rolls.

00:29:41.130 --> 00:29:43.840
We stayed at the Graduate
Hotel on Music Row,

00:29:43.840 --> 00:29:45.190
I don't know if you know about this place,

00:29:45.190 --> 00:29:49.180
but it's basically a
country music themed hotel

00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:50.771
that has some awesome decor

00:29:50.771 --> 00:29:54.222
and like pictures of
Dolly Parton in the lobby.

00:29:54.222 --> 00:29:55.055
Oh, that's cool.

00:29:55.055 --> 00:29:57.990
And your key, cards for
getting in and out of your room

00:29:57.990 --> 00:30:01.570
are like student IDs, I had
like Waylon Jennings' student ID

00:30:01.570 --> 00:30:02.903
and Johnny Cash's student ID.

00:30:02.903 --> 00:30:06.850
It's like what you have is
your key to open your door.

00:30:06.850 --> 00:30:07.940
Student ID.

00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:09.820
It is made up, it's not real.

00:30:09.820 --> 00:30:12.020
I don't think they ever had student IDs.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:15.890
Emmylou Harris, a portrait
of her was over my bed

00:30:17.222 --> 00:30:19.540
and I can't remember who was
Locke's bed, I've got pictures,

00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:21.260
you're probably seeing them at this point.

00:30:21.260 --> 00:30:22.610
But that was a fun experience.

00:30:22.610 --> 00:30:24.440
Also, shout out to the front desk,

00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:26.460
they're Mythical Beast at the Graduate,

00:30:26.460 --> 00:30:29.213
at least those that I
interacted with that night.

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:31.093
But we got on the next morning.

00:30:31.093 --> 00:30:32.880
Did you get a chocolate on your pillow,

00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:33.713
a night chocolate?

00:30:33.713 --> 00:30:35.283
They don't do that, it's
not a country music thing.

00:30:35.283 --> 00:30:37.183
I mean, for you.

00:30:37.183 --> 00:30:39.210
So next day we're up

00:30:39.210 --> 00:30:43.690
and the goal is to get
to Chester, Arkansas.

00:30:43.690 --> 00:30:44.870
Never heard of it.

00:30:44.870 --> 00:30:47.690
No reason to have heard of it until today.

00:30:47.690 --> 00:30:50.040
Hopefully, I'm going to give
you a reason to hear about it.

00:30:50.040 --> 00:30:52.080
But we were going to go through Memphis.

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:53.594
So we knew we were
going to stop in Memphis

00:30:53.594 --> 00:30:55.580
and again, I'm thinking about two things.

00:30:55.580 --> 00:30:56.413
I'm thinking about-

00:30:56.413 --> 00:30:57.246
Ribs and ribs.

00:30:57.246 --> 00:30:59.510
I'm thinking about stopping
at Central Barbecue,

00:30:59.510 --> 00:31:02.040
which has the best ribs we've ever had.

00:31:02.040 --> 00:31:03.660
If you remember the...

00:31:03.660 --> 00:31:04.493
I'm crying, man.

00:31:04.493 --> 00:31:06.500
On Memphis trip where we decided

00:31:06.500 --> 00:31:07.750
on what the best ribs were

00:31:07.750 --> 00:31:09.270
and it was clearly Central Barbecue?

00:31:09.270 --> 00:31:12.077
We wanted to stop there
but the downtown location

00:31:12.077 --> 00:31:14.900
is directly across the street
from the Civil Rights Museum,

00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:16.650
which is at the Lorraine
Hotel, which is where

00:31:16.650 --> 00:31:18.423
MLK was shot and killed.

00:31:19.560 --> 00:31:20.987
And I've never been in
there and I was like,

00:31:20.987 --> 00:31:23.690
"This'll be a cool thing
for father and son to do."

00:31:23.690 --> 00:31:25.740
We get to have this incredible meal

00:31:25.740 --> 00:31:28.740
and then we get essentially
some sobering US history

00:31:28.740 --> 00:31:30.860
in the middle of our trip,

00:31:30.860 --> 00:31:33.750
but it turns out that the
Central Barbecue location

00:31:33.750 --> 00:31:38.380
was closed at that for
some reason, it was closed.

00:31:38.380 --> 00:31:39.690
And I was like, well, I've
got my heart set on this

00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:41.280
so I had to drive 15 minutes

00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:42.852
to the original Central Barbecue location,

00:31:42.852 --> 00:31:46.296
which is on Central Avenue,
I didn't know about this.

00:31:46.296 --> 00:31:48.910
So, now I've seen the other one,

00:31:48.910 --> 00:31:50.760
it's a lot like the second one.

00:31:50.760 --> 00:31:54.660
So, you were at the MLK Museum,

00:31:54.660 --> 00:31:56.860
but since Central Barbecue was closed

00:31:57.736 --> 00:31:59.520
you didn't go in the museum.

00:31:59.520 --> 00:32:01.045
Well, it was lunchtime,
we were super hungry.

00:32:01.045 --> 00:32:01.878
You had get to Central Barbecue.

00:32:01.878 --> 00:32:04.460
And we wanted to spend a
couple of hours at the museum,

00:32:04.460 --> 00:32:07.920
I wasn't about to go
in there, we were also,

00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:09.260
we weren't eating breakfast,

00:32:09.260 --> 00:32:11.105
we were like getting a
coffee when we woke up

00:32:11.105 --> 00:32:13.823
and it was like, we're
going to, and we eat lunch.

00:32:15.130 --> 00:32:16.890
I've been doing like an
intermittent fasting thing

00:32:16.890 --> 00:32:18.670
and Locke is amenable
to pretty much anything

00:32:18.670 --> 00:32:20.560
so that's what we decided to do.

00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:22.630
It was also, you can kind of
get on the road and just go.

00:32:22.630 --> 00:32:26.103
So go to the original
Central Barbecue location.

00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:30.450
I got to say, I love Central Barbecue,

00:32:30.450 --> 00:32:33.950
but for me, the thing
that shines is the ribs

00:32:33.950 --> 00:32:36.470
and everything else is kinda
just like good barbecue,

00:32:36.470 --> 00:32:38.080
but not great barbecue.

00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:40.010
I don't remember if that
was your experience,

00:32:40.010 --> 00:32:41.480
if you remember.

00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:43.180
We were already so full when we got

00:32:43.180 --> 00:32:46.370
the spread from Central
Barbecue when we went there.

00:32:46.370 --> 00:32:47.510
We were on a rib mission.

00:32:47.510 --> 00:32:49.040
So, did the ribs hold true?

00:32:49.040 --> 00:32:50.661
The ribs are so good.

00:32:50.661 --> 00:32:51.494
Great, okay.

00:32:52.380 --> 00:32:54.690
I got ribs, pulled pork

00:32:54.690 --> 00:32:56.140
and I ordered chicken,

00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:57.640
I thought I was ordering
the smoked chicken,

00:32:57.640 --> 00:32:59.150
but they gave me the shredded chicken,

00:32:59.150 --> 00:33:02.150
like the pulled chicken,
it is a little dry.

00:33:02.150 --> 00:33:03.270
And again, I think I said that

00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:04.760
the rendezvous beans were better,

00:33:04.760 --> 00:33:06.010
I got beans and they're not bad,

00:33:06.010 --> 00:33:07.950
but it's really, Just get the ribs.

00:33:07.950 --> 00:33:09.940
If you're a rib person, get the ribs.

00:33:09.940 --> 00:33:12.810
But going back to the Civil Rights Museum,

00:33:12.810 --> 00:33:13.643
which, again...

00:33:13.643 --> 00:33:15.610
So, you did go back to
the Civil Rights Museum?

00:33:15.610 --> 00:33:16.443
Oh yeah,

00:33:16.443 --> 00:33:17.276
That's what I was asking.

00:33:17.276 --> 00:33:18.420
You seemed like you were just like,

00:33:18.420 --> 00:33:20.687
I have to make a choice and
it's going to be for ribs.

00:33:20.687 --> 00:33:22.360
No, no, no, I'm saying that...

00:33:22.360 --> 00:33:23.315
Okay, so you went back.

00:33:23.315 --> 00:33:24.148
we wanted to eat at Central Barbecue

00:33:24.148 --> 00:33:24.981
and then we were going go
back to Civil Rights Museum.

00:33:24.981 --> 00:33:26.460
Oh, I didn't know you went back.

00:33:26.460 --> 00:33:27.932
I mean, it's still in the same town.

00:33:27.932 --> 00:33:29.460
I'm driving across the country,

00:33:29.460 --> 00:33:30.800
15 minutes is not going to
be that big a difference.

00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:31.930
You're on an expedition.

00:33:31.930 --> 00:33:36.930
So, we go to the museum
and, listen, I mean,

00:33:37.280 --> 00:33:41.870
you can imagine the sort of
intensity of the experience

00:33:41.870 --> 00:33:43.010
of the Civil Rights Museum,

00:33:43.010 --> 00:33:47.690
but I can't really say
anything to communicate that.

00:33:47.690 --> 00:33:49.680
I just got to tell you
if you're in Memphis,

00:33:49.680 --> 00:33:50.850
you should go to it, right?

00:33:50.850 --> 00:33:54.380
And I think that the story of the hotel

00:33:54.380 --> 00:33:57.800
and how after he was
killed there on the balcony

00:34:00.210 --> 00:34:03.050
the story of the thing
falling into disrepair

00:34:03.050 --> 00:34:04.640
and then like local
leaders coming together

00:34:04.640 --> 00:34:06.680
and saying, "We wanna save this hotel."

00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:09.980
And then they literally
built the museum around it

00:34:09.980 --> 00:34:13.860
and inside of it, but kept
the two rooms right there,

00:34:13.860 --> 00:34:15.580
the one that he stayed
in and the one that,

00:34:15.580 --> 00:34:16.620
I think they had a meeting in,

00:34:16.620 --> 00:34:20.230
or the one he was shot in front
of, they kept them intact.

00:34:20.230 --> 00:34:21.605
And then they've added
some things of like,

00:34:21.605 --> 00:34:23.250
this is what would have been on the table

00:34:23.250 --> 00:34:24.850
and here's like the
ashtray with cigarettes

00:34:24.850 --> 00:34:27.230
that they may have been smoking and stuff,

00:34:27.230 --> 00:34:29.270
it's just a really well done museum

00:34:29.270 --> 00:34:30.510
that has so much information.

00:34:30.510 --> 00:34:32.090
I actually felt bad because

00:34:33.730 --> 00:34:36.630
there's so much information
to read and to digest

00:34:36.630 --> 00:34:38.800
and there's so many cool
things to watch and experience

00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:40.640
as you go through,

00:34:40.640 --> 00:34:41.733
but when you're on a road
trip and you're kind of like,

00:34:41.733 --> 00:34:44.802
we have to get to Chester,

00:34:44.802 --> 00:34:46.890
for reasons I'll get to in a second,

00:34:46.890 --> 00:34:50.130
so we actually only did like
two thirds of the museum.

00:34:50.130 --> 00:34:53.004
There's a whole other side,
which kind of goes underground

00:34:53.004 --> 00:34:55.040
and I think it goes up to the place

00:34:55.040 --> 00:34:57.200
where the shot was fired
or gets close to it.

00:34:57.200 --> 00:35:00.430
I didn't go in, so I'm
not sure, I'm speculating.

00:35:00.430 --> 00:35:04.790
But definitely recommend
that, and it was very,

00:35:04.790 --> 00:35:08.530
just seeing the spot, hearing the story

00:35:08.530 --> 00:35:10.440
and then standing up there right

00:35:10.440 --> 00:35:12.390
next to where he was shot is just like,

00:35:13.625 --> 00:35:16.933
it's a sobering experience for anyone.

00:35:17.810 --> 00:35:20.310
But then on to Chester, Arkansas.

00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:22.830
So that was what was kind of driving us

00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:26.840
to get to Nashville then to Memphis,

00:35:26.840 --> 00:35:28.800
then the Chester to spend the night.

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:32.690
So we talked a lot about Lance
and Lacey of Beard and Lady,

00:35:32.690 --> 00:35:35.940
some really good friends
of mine and of ours.

00:35:35.940 --> 00:35:40.588
Bearded lady makes all the
the mythical grooming products

00:35:40.588 --> 00:35:43.280
and also helped us kind of come
up with the idea originally

00:35:43.280 --> 00:35:45.860
for beard oil and lip
balm and all that stuff.

00:35:45.860 --> 00:35:49.580
Well, Lacey is from this area of Arkansas,

00:35:49.580 --> 00:35:52.940
which is right off of 40
as you're coming through

00:35:52.940 --> 00:35:54.780
because most of our trip was on 40.

00:35:54.780 --> 00:35:57.120
I mean, they're like literally
like 15 minutes from 40.

00:35:57.120 --> 00:35:58.627
So as soon as I'm mapping
through it, I'm like,

00:35:58.627 --> 00:36:00.000
"Hold on, this goes
right through Arkansas."

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.833
And then I was like,

00:36:00.833 --> 00:36:03.260
"This is like right next to
where they've got this hotel."

00:36:03.260 --> 00:36:06.990
So they have bought this historic

00:36:06.990 --> 00:36:10.680
100-year-old hotel in Chester,

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:13.483
which is a very teeny,
tiny town and they had...

00:36:13.483 --> 00:36:15.860
They built a museum around it?

00:36:15.860 --> 00:36:20.380
No, it's not like the
museum, they have restored it

00:36:20.380 --> 00:36:22.620
and it's called the Beard and Lady Inn,

00:36:22.620 --> 00:36:24.030
and it has three components.

00:36:24.030 --> 00:36:26.540
Number one, it's a hotel with 11 rooms,

00:36:26.540 --> 00:36:29.080
so it's kind of like a boutique hotel.

00:36:29.080 --> 00:36:30.980
I'll tell you about the rooms in a second,

00:36:30.980 --> 00:36:35.640
it also has a restaurant
that serves local Arkansas

00:36:35.640 --> 00:36:37.450
wild game and stuff.

00:36:37.450 --> 00:36:40.100
By the time this goes out
and you're listening to this,

00:36:40.100 --> 00:36:43.570
it will be, basically they're opening up

00:36:43.570 --> 00:36:45.550
the restaurant as we speak.

00:36:45.550 --> 00:36:47.850
All this information is
at beardandladyinn.com,

00:36:47.850 --> 00:36:49.330
but there's also a Mark and Tile.

00:36:49.330 --> 00:36:53.000
So like a store where they
sell mythical products,

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:56.250
but also a bunch of other
stuff from like local vendors.

00:36:56.250 --> 00:36:59.350
If you're like a Northwest Arkansas person

00:36:59.350 --> 00:37:01.430
and you've got something cool to sell,

00:37:01.430 --> 00:37:04.340
like there there's so much room
in this incredible facility

00:37:04.340 --> 00:37:05.660
they've set up that you can...

00:37:05.660 --> 00:37:08.683
And they're doing all
kinds of stuff there.

00:37:09.585 --> 00:37:11.800
I mean, I highly recommend
it if you're coming through,

00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:15.430
because it's definitely the
coolest place that we stayed.

00:37:15.430 --> 00:37:16.820
Even cooler than Graduate,

00:37:16.820 --> 00:37:19.240
just because of the history of this place.

00:37:19.240 --> 00:37:20.650
And also it's haunted.

00:37:20.650 --> 00:37:21.483
Is it?

00:37:21.483 --> 00:37:24.540
Yeah, so it has a reputation,
in fact, as they were,

00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:26.007
they bought this thing a couple years ago

00:37:26.007 --> 00:37:28.030
and then they slowly restored it

00:37:28.030 --> 00:37:31.063
and they said that locals
would come by and be like,

00:37:32.307 --> 00:37:34.070
"You seen a ghost yet?"

00:37:34.070 --> 00:37:37.490
Basically, this place is
notorious for being haunted.

00:37:37.490 --> 00:37:39.240
So, I think it also be a destination

00:37:39.240 --> 00:37:41.280
for paranormal seeking people.

00:37:41.280 --> 00:37:42.930
Doesn't that play into the theme?

00:37:42.930 --> 00:37:47.515
Yeah, so the theme of the rooms

00:37:47.515 --> 00:37:52.515
it's either fear of something
or it's just a general theme

00:37:53.330 --> 00:37:54.673
about a life experience.

00:37:55.550 --> 00:37:56.823
But it's kind of funny in that,

00:37:56.823 --> 00:38:00.880
I stayed in the fear of
commitment room, right?

00:38:00.880 --> 00:38:04.060
And so Lacey's family
history goes way, way back

00:38:04.060 --> 00:38:08.060
in that area and her grandparents
were incredible collectors

00:38:08.060 --> 00:38:11.920
or archivers of their family
history and pictures and stuff

00:38:11.920 --> 00:38:13.960
and so they've got these pictures

00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:15.790
in that room that I stayed in.

00:38:15.790 --> 00:38:18.410
There's all these pictures
of her grandparents

00:38:18.410 --> 00:38:20.660
and relatives in there, wedding portraits

00:38:20.660 --> 00:38:22.640
and pictures of them together
throughout the years.

00:38:22.640 --> 00:38:26.480
All this old, like 10 type old school,

00:38:26.480 --> 00:38:28.480
black and white photography,
and everything's...

00:38:28.480 --> 00:38:30.540
Basically, it tells a story of commitment.

00:38:30.540 --> 00:38:31.373
Yeah, so it's like,

00:38:31.373 --> 00:38:33.220
"Okay, if you've got fear of commitments,

00:38:33.220 --> 00:38:34.890
let's see all these people around you

00:38:34.890 --> 00:38:37.320
that are committed to one another."

00:38:37.320 --> 00:38:39.373
Interestingly, one of the rooms,

00:38:39.373 --> 00:38:42.123
which I think it might be fear of death,

00:38:43.693 --> 00:38:45.520
you can go on the website
and see all the rooms,

00:38:45.520 --> 00:38:49.690
but her great-grandparents

00:38:49.690 --> 00:38:52.780
are the only people known on record,

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:57.051
at least on record at the
time, to request a dual coffin.

00:38:57.051 --> 00:38:57.884
What?

00:38:57.884 --> 00:39:01.030
They died within hours of each other

00:39:01.030 --> 00:39:03.860
and the dual coffin was made for them.

00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:07.660
And there's pictures of them
in the coffin, all in the room.

00:39:07.660 --> 00:39:08.880
What?

00:39:08.880 --> 00:39:09.800
It's incredible.

00:39:09.800 --> 00:39:12.153
So is it, okay, first of all,

00:39:15.583 --> 00:39:18.057
how did they die so closely?

00:39:18.057 --> 00:39:20.420
Because I guess the first
thing I thought was,

00:39:20.420 --> 00:39:22.620
okay, one of them dies, you bury them

00:39:22.620 --> 00:39:23.510
then you've got to dig them up

00:39:23.510 --> 00:39:24.710
and throw the other person in there?

00:39:24.710 --> 00:39:25.770
Yeah, I think it was...

00:39:25.770 --> 00:39:27.007
They were counting on
dying at the same time?

00:39:27.007 --> 00:39:30.490
I think that the circumstances led to,

00:39:30.490 --> 00:39:32.830
she died or he, one of them died first,

00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:34.610
and the other one knew that
they were about to die.

00:39:34.610 --> 00:39:35.576
I can't remember,

00:39:35.576 --> 00:39:36.700
the story of the same disease or whatever.

00:39:36.700 --> 00:39:37.970
Throw us in the same coffin.

00:39:37.970 --> 00:39:40.480
I think it was like a last
minute request like that

00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.237
and they totally did it, it was crazy.

00:39:42.237 --> 00:39:43.710
Was it a wider coffin?

00:39:43.710 --> 00:39:45.100
Yeah, it's shaped like a square.

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:46.300
It's like a square coffin.

00:39:46.300 --> 00:39:47.133
What?

00:39:47.133 --> 00:39:49.130
Yeah and there's pictures of them in it.

00:39:49.130 --> 00:39:50.270
Dead bodies in it?

00:39:50.270 --> 00:39:52.000
Yeah, but you don't have
to stay in that room,

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:53.420
it's all about your level of comfort.

00:39:53.420 --> 00:39:56.943
And there's one room that is
known as, the Haunted Room.

00:39:58.260 --> 00:40:01.860
First of all, the whole place
is potentially haunted, right?

00:40:01.860 --> 00:40:04.670
But there's one room that
is right above the place

00:40:04.670 --> 00:40:08.364
where a guy once like froze
to death in this little,

00:40:08.364 --> 00:40:11.277
I think this saloon
that was attached to it.

00:40:11.277 --> 00:40:15.610
Again, all these stories in
more detail are on the website,

00:40:15.610 --> 00:40:18.170
but I didn't stay in
that room, but we walked,

00:40:18.170 --> 00:40:20.880
they're just opening and so
there was one other couple

00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:22.090
that was staying there that night

00:40:22.090 --> 00:40:23.310
and then it was me and Locke

00:40:23.310 --> 00:40:25.033
and we stayed in enjoining rooms.

00:40:26.920 --> 00:40:28.460
Lance and Lacey's history of

00:40:28.460 --> 00:40:30.280
traveling multiple
times to the Middle East

00:40:30.280 --> 00:40:31.300
over the 20's and 30's

00:40:31.300 --> 00:40:35.011
and they've got all these like artifacts

00:40:35.011 --> 00:40:37.644
and like a camel saddle
and all this stuff,

00:40:37.644 --> 00:40:39.460
that was connected to my room.

00:40:39.460 --> 00:40:41.700
So the Middle East room, which
is not a fear of anything,

00:40:41.700 --> 00:40:43.240
it's just a Middle East theme room,

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:44.820
and then I was in the
fear of commitment room,

00:40:44.820 --> 00:40:46.220
and then there's a
bathroom attached to that

00:40:46.220 --> 00:40:48.300
and so we were kind of
had enjoining rooms.

00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:49.460
Okay.

00:40:49.460 --> 00:40:52.210
But it's really hard for
me to convey how cool

00:40:52.210 --> 00:40:54.360
and unusual of a space it is

00:40:54.360 --> 00:40:55.360
and the thing that they're trying to do

00:40:55.360 --> 00:40:58.910
because it's on the railroad

00:40:58.910 --> 00:41:01.340
and they're currently basically lobbying

00:41:01.340 --> 00:41:02.910
to get it added as a stop

00:41:02.910 --> 00:41:05.810
so you can be in one of
the major city centers

00:41:05.810 --> 00:41:08.984
that's close by north and
south and you can take a train

00:41:08.984 --> 00:41:12.090
and it will let you off.

00:41:12.090 --> 00:41:15.370
And they've also bought a church,

00:41:15.370 --> 00:41:20.030
this 100-year-old church
in a nearby place that,

00:41:20.030 --> 00:41:21.357
the whole idea is that people,

00:41:21.357 --> 00:41:22.970
and I think this is already,

00:41:22.970 --> 00:41:24.330
they've had a couple of wedding parties,

00:41:24.330 --> 00:41:26.980
because it's a really cool
thing to run the whole hotel

00:41:26.980 --> 00:41:29.490
and have an event.

00:41:29.490 --> 00:41:31.277
And they bought this church

00:41:31.277 --> 00:41:32.890
and the idea is that in the future people

00:41:32.890 --> 00:41:35.820
will get married at this venue,

00:41:35.820 --> 00:41:36.900
And then dine in the hotel.

00:41:36.900 --> 00:41:38.950
and then go to the hotel.

00:41:38.950 --> 00:41:42.000
And again, if you're into
paranormal stuff, it's great.

00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.020
If you're not, there's plenty of options

00:41:44.020 --> 00:41:46.360
and plenty of rooms to
stay in that are not,

00:41:46.360 --> 00:41:51.360
but it was one of the
coolest stops that we made.

00:41:51.430 --> 00:41:54.837
And then it kind of took us
on a tour of the family land

00:41:54.837 --> 00:41:57.240
and some other stuff the next morning

00:41:57.240 --> 00:42:01.040
and we got to see some
of Northwest Arkansas,

00:42:01.040 --> 00:42:02.975
which is a special place, special place.

00:42:02.975 --> 00:42:05.460
Special place, huh? Hilly?

00:42:05.460 --> 00:42:09.560
Yeah, actually it's pretty mountainous.

00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:10.690
I would call it,

00:42:10.690 --> 00:42:12.540
it feels like you're in the
North Carolina mountains.

00:42:12.540 --> 00:42:14.749
And I mean, essentially I think

00:42:14.749 --> 00:42:16.105
it's a different mountain range.

00:42:16.105 --> 00:42:18.136
because it's like the Ozarks.

00:42:18.136 --> 00:42:22.290
But it has that feel of
like very wooded mountains

00:42:22.290 --> 00:42:23.560
that you just feel like you get lost

00:42:23.560 --> 00:42:25.020
and lots of lakes and stuff.

00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:26.480
Lots of streams and rivers.

00:42:26.480 --> 00:42:27.700
That's cool.

00:42:27.700 --> 00:42:28.533
But I didn't see...

00:42:28.533 --> 00:42:29.490
That would be night two.

00:42:29.490 --> 00:42:30.791
Yeah, I didn't see anything.

00:42:30.791 --> 00:42:32.063
No ghosts?

00:42:32.063 --> 00:42:33.900
I didn't see any ghosts
and I was very open to it.

00:42:33.900 --> 00:42:36.360
And I was like standing in there at night,

00:42:36.360 --> 00:42:37.690
sort of staring into the mirror

00:42:37.690 --> 00:42:39.330
waiting for things to happen.

00:42:39.330 --> 00:42:40.554
I was embracing it, I was like,

00:42:40.554 --> 00:42:41.387
